\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {13}{\ignorespaces Coleman-Weinberg effective potential $V_{CW}(\theta )$ for the MAP benchmark. \textbf  {Left}: Full potential over $\theta \in [0^\circ , 180^\circ ]$, showing the minimum near $\theta = 90^\circ $ (maximal CP violation). The $A_4$ symmetry discretizes the minimum to $\theta _{relic} = 18.43^\circ $. \textbf  {Right}: Zoom near the relic angle. The green region ($\theta < \theta _{relic}$) is DM-dominated; the purple region ($\theta > \theta _{relic}$) contributes to dark energy. The universe sits at the purple dot --- a non-zero CP angle that simultaneously satisfies SIDM and relic constraints.}}{25}{figure.109}\protected@file@percent }
